 The BFD 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Brendan Lynch/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Saudi Arabia's Public Investment Fund is weighing a merger of video game makers Electronic Arts and Savvy Games , per Bloomberg.

 Why it's the BFD: Gamers might be close to a mash-up of Madden and Pokémon GO.

 Catch up quick: PIF recently led a $55 billion take-private acquisition of EA , with Silver Lake and Affinity Partners also participating.

 Five years ago PIF created Savvy as a video game platform, later buying assets like Scopely and Niantic's games unit. Yes, but: None of the aforementioned deals sparked major antitrust scrutiny, but this one likely would.

 The bottom line: "Such a combination would represent a major shift in the structure of the Saudi sovereign wealth fund's gaming strategy, potentially giving it a single vehicle through which to make acquisitions, develop games and exploit intellectual property across different parts of the $214 billion industry." — Dinesh Nair &amp; Cecilia D'Anastasio, Bloomberg 

 
 
